# Line endings are part of this repository's contract. Component bytes,
# report identities, and digest checks bind the exact bytes of tracked files
# (sources and WIT through `include_str!`, the vendored XSD and fixtures through
# `include_bytes!`, the IRP corpora (the W3C and each namespace suite) and
# their baselines through recorded SHA-256
# digests), so no checkout may rewrite them, whatever `core.autocrlf` says.

# Authored text: always LF in the working tree, and CRLF is normalized to LF
# on commit so an editor that writes CRLF cannot change the stored bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-pinned trees: stored and checked out verbatim, never converted in
# either direction. Their bytes are recorded upstream bytes or blessed
# expected output, and any conversion is a digest or snapshot failure.
crates/scxml-validator-xsd/schemas/** -text
tests/conformance/** -text
tests/fixtures/** -text
tests/ui/** -text
namespaces/*/irp/** -text
